{"step_index":1842,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T13:30:42Z","input_tokens":2068,"cache_read_tokens":214671,"output_tokens":127,"content":"Understood—**OSCAL subcategory taxonomy**, not subvolumes! \n\nThe subcategory taxonomy classifies operations by their operational intent (`mut.*` for mutations, `obs.*` for observations/reads, `src.*` for sources, etc.), and by making that taxonomy its own plugin, any plugin automatically inherits those subcategories and their compliance review metadata.\n\nThe same applies to Ethereum: an **on-chain settlement subcategory taxonomy** (e.g. `settle.*`, `escrow.*`, `attest.*`) that plugins inherit so operations can declare their smart contract settlement intent directly in their schema."}
